{
  "summary": "Parallelizes BIP 157/158 compact block filter checks during wallet fast rescans across worker threads. Introduces the -walletpar configuration option (defaulting to auto-detected CPU cores up to 15 dedicated worker threads) to control wallet concurrency. Filter checks are queued and evaluated in parallel while block reading, block syncing, and keypool top-ups remain serialized on the calling thread, with parallel rescanning disabled during Initial Block Download.",
  "problem": "Compact block filter evaluation during fast wallet rescans executes sequentially on a single core. On multi-core machines, rescanning large block spans—such as during descriptor imports or wallet restores—leaves available CPU resources idle and takes several minutes.",
  "evidence": [
    "Author's mainnet benchmark scanning 200,000 blocks (heights 700,000 to 900,000) on an empty wallet demonstrates a runtime drop from 272 seconds on master (and 274s at 1 thread) to ~38 seconds with 8 threads and ~25 seconds with 16 threads."
  ],
