  "changed_since_previous": "Added a check to fall back to serial fast rescan during Initial Block Download to avoid core contention with block validation. Increased MAX_WALLETPAR from 8 to 15 dedicated worker threads. Ensured a block's active chain status is validated under cs_wallet before syncing transactions to avoid race conditions with block disconnection. Added functional and unit tests covering IBD behavior and mid-chain startup rescans.",
  "card": "Parallelizes BIP 157/158 compact block filter evaluation during wallet fast rescans across worker threads. Introduces the -walletpar configuration option to control wallet concurrency, auto-detecting core count up to 15 worker threads by default while falling back to serial rescan during Initial Block Download. Fast wallet rescans previously checked block filters sequentially on a single thread, causing wallet restores and rescans to take minutes over long block ranges. On author benchmarks scanning 200,000 mainnet blocks, runtime dropped from 272 seconds serially to 38 seconds at 8 threads and 25 seconds at 16 threads.",
